-- title:
--   Binary forms vanishing on 𝔽ₚ² are divisible by Dickson's invariant
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime (supplied as a `Fact` instance), let $K$ be a field of characteristic $p$, and let $n$ be a natural number. Let $F \in K[X_0,X_1]$ (a polynomial in the two variables indexed by `Fin 2`) lie in [`HeckeEis.BinaryForm K n`](def/HeckeEis_BinaryFormRep.html#L25), that is, in the submodule `MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 2) K n` of forms all of whose monomials have total degree $n$. Assume that $F$ vanishes at every $\mathbb{F}_p$-point: for every $v : \mathrm{Fin}\ 2 \to \mathbb{Z}/p$, the evaluation of $F$ at the coordinates $\mathrm{ZMod.castHom}\ (\mathrm{dvd\_refl}\ p)\ K\,(v\,i)$, the images of $v$ under the canonical ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Z}/p \to K$, is $0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $H \in K[X_0,X_1]$ which is homogeneous of degree $n - (p+1)$, the subtraction being truncated subtraction of natural numbers, such that $$F = (X_0^{\,p}X_1 - X_0X_1^{\,p})\cdot H.$$ In particular, when $n \le p$ the degree $n-(p+1)$ is $0$, so $H$ is a constant and comparison of degrees in the displayed identity forces $F = 0$.
--
--   The factor $X_0^pX_1 - X_0X_1^p$ is Dickson's invariant, the product up to sign of the $p+1$ pairwise non-proportional linear forms with coefficients in $\mathbb{F}_p$; the statement says that the kernel of the evaluation map from binary forms of degree $n$ to $K$-valued functions on $\mathbb{F}_p^2$ is contained in the ideal generated by this invariant. It is used in [`HeckeEis.exists_filtration_binaryForm_subquotient_le_sub_one`](thm.html#HeckeEis.exists_filtration_binaryForm_subquotient_le_sub_one) to control the subquotients of the filtration of spaces of binary forms by such vanishing conditions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HeckeEis_exists_binaryForm_eq_mul_of_forall_eval_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_HeckeEis_BinaryFormRep

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open MvPolynomial in

theorem HeckeEis.exists_binaryForm_eq_mul_of_forall_eval_eq_zero (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]
    (K : Type*) [Field K] [CharP K p] (n : ℕ) (F : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K)
    (hF : F ∈ HeckeEis.BinaryForm K n)
    (hvan : ∀ v : Fin 2 → ZMod p,
      MvPolynomial.eval (fun i => ZMod.castHom (dvd_refl p) K (v i)) F = 0) :
    ∃ H : MvPolynomial (Fin 2) K, H ∈ HeckeEis.BinaryForm K (n - (p + 1)) ∧
      F = (X 0 ^ p * X 1 - X 0 * X 1 ^ p) * H := by sorry
